					<item>
		<title><![CDATA[Sleep: the recovery tool most people ignore]]></title>
		<link>http://localhost:8080/sleep-the-recovery-tool-most-people-ignore/</link>
		<pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 03:58:47 +0000</pubDate>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[ironpeak-admin]]></dc:creator>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://localhost:8080/sleep-the-recovery-tool-most-people-ignore/</guid>
		<description></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Members often ask us which supplement to buy. Our first answer is always the same: are you sleeping 7 to 9 hours a night?</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Why it matters
Deep sleep is when your body releases most of its growth hormone and repairs the muscle you broke down in training. Short sleep also raises hunger hormones, which makes fat loss harder.</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Simple habits that help
Keep a fixed bedtime, even on weekends. Put your phone away 30 minutes before sleep. Avoid tea or coffee after 4 pm. Keep your room dark and cool.</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">The bottom line
No program or protein powder can make up for poor sleep. Fix this first and everything else in the gym gets easier.</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->]]></content:encoded>
		<excerpt:encoded><![CDATA[You can train hard and eat well, but without 7 to 9 hours of sleep your results will stall. Here is why sleep matters so much.]]></excerpt:encoded>
